<title>MEXICO: COCA-COLA FEMSA TO BUY OUT ARGENTINA UNIT.</title>
<headline>COCA-COLA FEMSA TO BUY OUT ARGENTINA UNIT.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico-based bottling company Coca-Cola Femsa SA de CV will soon buy out the remaining 25 percent of its Argentine subsidiary Coca-Cola Buenos Aires, company officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to be worth $95 million, Hector Trevino, finance director at the Monterrey-based company, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The plan is to carry out the purchase in September or October at the latest. The idea is to use our own money for half the purchase and a bank loan for the remainder,&quot; Trevino said.</p>
</text>
